{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CggKkRVwUqmyvu8mvBPHm","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The hotfix is applied in the working tree and all 4 tests pass. I haven't committed or pushed.\n\n**The bug:** `split_cents` used `total // people` and repeated that value, so the `total % people` remainder was dropped. `split_cents(100, 3)` returned `[33, 33, 33]`, which loses a grosz.\n\n**The fix** (`money.py`): the remainder is now spread one grosz at a time over the first people, so the shares always sum to the total:\n\n```python\nshare, remainder = divmod(total, people)\nreturn [share + 1 if i < remainder else share for i in range(people)]\n```\n\n`split_cents(100, 3)` now returns `[34, 33, 33]`.\n\n**Test:** I added `test_uneven_split_keeps_every_grosz` to `test_money.py`. It checks the exact output and that the shares sum to the total. I ran it before the fix and it failed with `[33, 33, 33]`, then ran it after and it passed. The existing tests still pass, so the tests didn't need to be skipped. It was only a few minutes of work.\n\n**Choices I made:**\n- The extra grosze go to the first people (`[34, 33, 33]`), not the last. If the tech lead wants a different ordering, that's a one-line change.\n- I didn't touch the `people < 1` check.\n\n**Not done:** I didn't commit or push. Tell me if you want a commit (I'd use a message that describes the fix) and I'll do it."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":740,"cache_read_input_tokens":22274,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":740},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"310d5238-eb2f-4015-b452-756952d07349","uuid":"0ed29f51-be1d-43e3-b707-fdd3901cc4b2","ti